@startuml article-lifecycle
title Presserl – Article Lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans-Serif
hide empty description

[*] --> Draft : new article

Draft --> Published : publish\n[no approval level remains]
Draft --> Submitted : publish\n[an approval level applies]
Submitted --> Submitted : approve\n[next level applies]
Submitted --> Published : approve\n[last level]
Submitted --> Draft : reject with note
Submitted --> Draft : withdraw (author)

Published --> Offline : take offline\n(author, section editor,\neditor-in-chief)
Published --> Locked : emergency brake\n(publisher)
Offline --> Published : back online\n[approval chain]
Offline --> Submitted : back online\n[approval chain]
Locked --> Offline : release\n(publisher only)
Offline --> Draft : revise
Offline --> [*] : delete

Submitted : waits for one level:
Submitted : section editor → editor-in-chief → publisher
Published : Edits create a new revision;
Published : the live revision stays until
Published : the new one passes the chain.
Locked : offline, only a publisher
Locked : can release it

note right of Draft
  Simplest case (first account, all roles):
  Draft → Published → Offline
  One click, no approval.
end note
@enduml
